We manually selected six high-order terms from the three Gene Ontology (accessed on 2024-01-17) sections: molecular function, biological process, cell component. The embeddings from P3GPT (N dimensions = 365), OpenBioLLM-8B (N dim = 4096), BioGPT-Large (N dim = 1600), Gemma-2B (N dim = 2048), Llama3-8B (N dim = 4096) were extracted using local instances of these LLMs installed from their Hugging Face repositories. For each gene embedding, binary prediction targets were defined as the presence of an ontology term in its annotation.
The embeddings of all genes were submitted to a CatBoost regressor training pipeline with 2000 iterations to predict whether a gene had a particular term with the following settings. The standard deviation of the reported ROC-AUC was measured based on CatBoost performance in five-fold crossvalidation.
