P3GPT-derived geroprotectors
P3GPT-mediated geroprotector generation
The geroprotector generation experiment was conducted using P3GPT models in a two-phase process:
1. Gene Expression Profiling: regulated genes for human lung tissue at the expression level. This was accomplished using the <age2diff> instruction protocol and specifying the case-control generation conditions as
Initially, Precious3GPT models were employed to generate lists of up-regulated and downolder adults (70-80 years) and younger adults (20-30 years), respectively;
2. Compound Identification : expression signature, the up-regulated and down-regulated gene lists were interchanged
Subsequently, the gene lists produced in Phase-1 were utilized as input for the P3GPT models' <diff2compound> instruction. To induce a reversal of the age-related gene prior to input. The IMR90 cell line, which served as the experimental model for in vitro studies, was specified as an additional parameter in the model input for this phase.
This two-step approach facilitated the identification of potential geroprotective compounds that could theoretically counteract age-associated gene expression changes in human lung tissue. On manual review, addictive, highly toxic, and commercially unavailable compounds were removed from consideration, resulting in a list of 22 compounds to be screened in an in vitro IMR90 model of induced senescence.

