All the aforementioned values were calculated in replicates of three for each dilution of the screened compounds. The statistical significance of non-zero action coefficients was assessed with MannWhithey's U-test.
Effectively, the senolytic action of a compound represents the drop in cell survival when senescence is induced. The senomorphic action represents the decrease in the relative number of senescent cells in response to compound exposure. The senomorphic test also requires that a compound does not decrease the total cell count in the ßPIX siRNA-treated cultures, which would imply cytotoxicity and/or senolytic action. The cytotoxic action of a compound represents the decrease in cell survival when senescence is not induced.
