5 Experiments
5.1 Configuration
Datasets. We conduct experiments on the proposed CellPuzzles . Each instance comprises 8 ≤ N ≤ 15 cells, each represented by its ranked top-expressed genes and a shared donor-level contextual description. For training, we perform reasoning distillation using a strong reasoning model to generate 3,912 high-quality reasoning traces, which are then used for SFT. In addition, we sample 3,000 extra instances to construct an RL dataset, resulting in a total of 6,912 instances for the GRPO stage. A held-out test set of 1,095 batches is used for final evaluation. More details on the dataset processing can be found in the Supplementary Materials.
Evaluation Metrics. We report results using the following metrics: (1) Cell-level Accuracy: The average proportion of correctly predicted labels per batch. (2) Batch-level Accuracy: The proportion of batches where all predicted labels exactly match the ground truth. (3) Format Validity: The proportion of outputs that follow the required response format. (4) Answer Uniqueness: The average proportion of unique cell type predictions per batch.

